  "description": "Emily turned 14, Carol bought\nher a Finest. Carol didn't know that Finest is a time-honored Fuji model\nname, nor did she study the specs and decide the Finest was just what\nEm needed. Em liked looking at the white and blue bike and Carol could\nafford it. Simple as that.\n\nThere are perfectly good, logical reasons to pick a Finest out of the\nherd of similarly priced bicycles. The Finest frame is made from good\nCro-Moly steel; it'll ride well and last for years and years. That frame\nhas eyelets for putting on fenders, a rear rack or saddlebag mounts. The\nframe will never limit the uses of the bike.\n\nThe parts on the Finest's frame are well-chosen Shimano ones. Emily liked\nthe three chainrings, the feeling that her bike also wasn't limited by\nits gearing or equipment. She even liked the saddle that came on her new\nbike. Really.\n\nEmily's been pedaling with her mom on local club rides, hanging in just\nfine. Probably the Finest is a bit finer than Emily needs now, but she'll\ngrow as a cyclist and it'll be perfect. Maybe she and Carol will tour\non their bikes this summer. Maybe someone will get a shot of them and\nwe'll run it in next year's catalog.",
